name: Link Analysis showcase
tagline: "A seeded Link Analysis demo - mule transfers with a planted ring, three landed days, staged next-day and gap-day files, five Demo Users, an index that builds itself and standing detection"
description: "The Link Analysis demo as a Space Template (LA-DEMO-SEED-1). One daily Collector + Pipeline + Dataset of synthetic account-to-account transfers (data/inbox: three landed days; data/staged: a next-day file and a gap-day file you copy into the inbox by hand). The planted story: 12 SMURF accounts structure cash into MULE-HUB-01, which passes it on through RELAY-01/02 to OFFSHORE-77; SHELL-A to SHELL-D circulate money in a loop; TILL-06 takes 80 percent of the cash-out; SKIMMER-01 skims benefit payments. The Suspicion score ranks MULE-HUB-01 in the top 3 and the ring is the only directed cycle. Settings: link-analysis.toon (masking typed, a low four-eyes fan-out threshold so expanding the hub waits for a second person, the link index ON, Drafts limits). Jobs: la_index_build (after every committed batch of the mule feed) and la_detect (every 5 minutes). Three saved views. Demo Users and their roles (roles.toon, demo-users.toon): fm.analyst (lead; Author Alert Rules), fm.manager (second approver), ra.analyst (reviewer, read-only), demo.manager (not a member), admin (reveal). Investigations, members, Entity Lists, a Case and a bound Alert Rule are runtime state with no template home: run `node tools/seed-la-showcase.mjs --apply` against the running server (docs/okf/capabilities/spaces/spaces.md, section la-showcase). TELECOM corpus (config/telecom, data/inbox/<feed>; regenerate with tools/gen-la-telecom-data.py): eight 60-day feeds (voice_cdr, sms_cdr, hlr_eir, crm_kyc, recharge, provisioning, fraud_blocklist, fraud_alarms) over 2 400 background subscribers with one planted ring per typology (Wangiri, IRSF, SIM box, subscription fraud, mules) and a 650-caller supernode; the telecom_links Job folds them into one MSISDN-to-MSISDN link Dataset (seven link kinds) and telecom_msisdn_indicators scores every MSISDN 0-100; the suspect 99979100001 reaches the SIM box at degree 4 (docs/superpower/la-telecom-demo-data.md). Needs a Professional or Enterprise edition build with the Link Analysis modules and the Demo Auth build (serve-demo). Synthetic data only."
icon: heroicons_outline:share
contents[10]: "Pipeline + schema (daily partition) with 3 landed days", "Dataset", "3 saved views", "8 telecom Pipelines with 60-day extracts and planted fraud rings", "telecom_links + telecom_msisdn_indicators Jobs, Datasets and a saved view", "link-analysis.toon (masking, four-eyes, index ON, Drafts)", "la_index_build Job (on pipeline.commit)", "la_detect Job (cron)", "5 Demo Users + role table", "Staged next-day and gap-day files"
